ion/math-academy-id "q-123753" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\,\\,\\,y=3t+2,\\,-2\\le t\\le 2,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $a$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=1-(-1)^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=3t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=3(0)+2=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=1-(2)^{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+2+(-3)=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123753/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-6834"] :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x={t}^{2}-4.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=(-1)^{2}-4=1-4=-3.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=5$ into $y=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b+c=-3-2+0=-5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "4dd08c63-9faa-58ca-98f5-47c32a6e9895" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a8280a04-e85c-5743-891f-abfd37c14739" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2e28290f-04bd-5b21-a4da-acfcbfe0c586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "1fac5e84-4bd3-590f-9218-3fb02402753f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "ab116900-23b9-5ab3-9a99-64314e877b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e55943b5-2e2f-5c6f-90d2-7ece1f243a23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-6742/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-6742/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-6742/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-6742/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-6742/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-6742/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6742" :question/id #uuid "43acae2f-c357-56e4-b21a-0bf699c0c709" :question/math-academy-id "q-6742" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-6,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $b$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=(-3)^{2}-6=9-6=3.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb={0}^{2}-6=0-6=-6.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=3+1=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=3-(-6)-4=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-6742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d2c4babc-f016-555f-95f6-24e4320c9d0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "6a948c48-01de-58fa-9dfb-933a17d01e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "46013532-a405-5c62-85be-c220efe3cf22" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326256/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-326256/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-326256/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "638a3879-8b9e-5686-bedb-77f7c8732fa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2a0c3c-2012-5456-aa8a-b3f41c4c8eec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326256/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-326256/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-3/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "cae88c29-ef32-5409-8407-90990777ecb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "99ba54f9-b6f6-56e6-b8f8-f4a7db344f85" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326256/field-3/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer-field/choices ["q-326256/field-3/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326256" :question/id #uuid "4cc20620-c2d3-5cb5-adf6-4d97890f6861" :question/math-academy-id "q-326256" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,y=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),\\,-1\\le t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(0),$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(0)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (0)}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(1)=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi (1)}{3})=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (2)}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-326256/field-1" "q-326256/field-2" "q-326256/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "d1a526b0-6ceb-553c-ae95-84b0ce05871c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0064fb-c987-5cb6-88d1-98c208ae2570" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326242/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-326242/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242/field-2/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "6720d6ed-a4b4-559b-acce-c6d66e5cf707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "83cf9500-d3a8-5900-a83e-e42277cd333a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326242/field-2/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-326242/field-2/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242/field-3/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" :answer/id #uuid "0b138873-6644-5893-8633-49c3e42ea4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8af02ca-12c5-5bcf-bb12-b6ea86475d9a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326242/field-3/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" :answer-field/choices ["q-326242/field-3/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326242" :question/id #uuid "04af7c3e-29ba-55d1-9de5-2657b1fa8459" :question/math-academy-id "q-326242" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{2}t+1,\\,y=-\\frac{5}{4}t+2,\\,-1\\le t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $7$ |\n| $y$ | {{field-3}} | $2$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{4}$ | $-3$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=\\frac{3}{2}t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)+1=-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=-\\frac{5}{4}t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(-1)=-\\frac{5}{4}(-1)+2=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{8}{4}=\\frac{13}{4}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=\\frac{3}{2}t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=\\frac{3}{2}(3)+1=\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $4$ | $\\frac{11}{2}$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{13}{4}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{4}$ | $-3$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-326242/field-1" "q-326242/field-2" "q-326242/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326242"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123780/selection/7336f60c868d6c907500e3c3b24d04e52d914637aeb81ab3979fb79a020fa916" :answer/id #uuid "f706bfcc-f755-5c59-9d9d-ad5619def5ed" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/a65650567b28f4d4dc9275c100d960208413423f031ee74b59496377562f84fa.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123780/selection/3aa9a7e19240e76eb9a73f5e3b8c726556f5e7005172bd6de17023919f099d7a" :answer/id #uuid "e9243ec1-60fd-5738-94a7-851b42f9ef86" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/ccdac60d2d9e7820ea4053977be2b71c4ffa18a8683c3bc9ef0752e806c0ffcd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123780/selection/a5dd34b97e206be6c03af16e4f3badd647183f9e25af7caaeb00a886703930bd" :answer/id #uuid "afc18c20-d372-5dc9-9a3f-ba05f1bc165e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/7cca3671544acd472c82651d3406347ce7e8c24aa4312096fcf7a1014bd1cdd1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123780/selection/88abd06499fad9c30de4dbafb46315a1b28a3ed6facbff3654abc0e32765ca35" :answer/id #uuid "b4341024-5f44-55e1-b25d-6f57202e36e0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/f65b8e725f7e4a81050d299b4edb8ade15ce5408a16d0d9849c4fa49c0c75985.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123780/selection/2a03c3bb8df941462112294e4a84890f71b2ca64377c7b31ad1d6fc742061d96" :answer/id