 out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y={t}^{2}-5.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/a9d9be86049e1422d9c5c7e4af24992959637c3771503b13f75865840076149b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326305/field-1/75e59402446e822899647eed82d1188ef6940397b9c8e57a93b6fb2cc311c639" :answer/id #uuid "8c61ef48-0185-5262-be2b-e8b45d2a040e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\geq" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326305/field-1/0611b43f7217be4eb0f20ccd4aabde227c6ba110eb6f464d2d666990873286ab" :answer/id #uuid "7a214fa4-411a-5089-a292-840a2c7f57f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\leq" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326305/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6091f5-8534-5e13-a093-7b7411a34aeb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326305/field-1/75e59402446e822899647eed82d1188ef6940397b9c8e57a93b6fb2cc311c639" :answer-field/choices ["q-326305/field-1/75e59402446e822899647eed82d1188ef6940397b9c8e57a93b6fb2cc311c639" "q-326305/field-1/0611b43f7217be4eb0f20ccd4aabde227c6ba110eb6f464d2d66699