on/id #uuid "30b04f17-aee8-5e9e-9e8e-8855a22f81b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-326305" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2}-4t,\\,y=(t-1)^{2}+2,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{t}^{2}-4t \\\\  & =2({t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =2({t}^{2}-2t+1)-2 \\\\  & =2(t-1)^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2(t-1)^{2}-2\\ge -2,$ we conclude that the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge -2.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that $(t-1)^{2}+2\\ge 2.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-326305/field-1" "q-326305/field-2" "q-326305/field-3" "q-326305/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326305"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123767/selection/724f1e88a01800fe18fa7944ab9c7918cccb2e85485fbbd6be305119b2a24441" :answer/id #uuid "b017aae2-e626-5e99-a5a0-31b4b61e867a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123767/selection/473e890d75efeb17e26c98feffd322f20fc5f93da18ffcbcca67deb849fd24a9" :answer/id #uuid "4e2e46fa-845d-5d2a-9713-4edf129f2a99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123767/selection/c168c0102e780a8650354780d63c76e56804b5637dd3d7264c050b551f6cf956" :answer/id #uuid "40192662-5865-5218-9c2e-334a4e93b7ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123767/selection/bab68388fca6f104bef4b9e2cdce499452d528f68cf829a342867b260c35c99d" :answer/id #uuid "d25af62e-d94f-55c4-a74f-322857e39