75f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-276257/field-4/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276257" :question/id #uuid "650a1759-ce40-5619-a3a2-2fcff9d9f46b" :question/math-academy-id "q-276257" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=5-4t,\\,y=t+1,\\,t\\ge -1.\n$$\n\nDetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=5-4t\\le 9$ for all $t\\ge -1.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 9.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $y=t+1\\ge 0$ for all $t\\ge -1.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-276257/field-1" "q-276257/field-2" "q-276257/field-3" "q-276257/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
